# Local app configuration. No private keys or API secrets are needed.
# Shell example: PORT=3000 npm run dev
PORT=3000
HOST=127.0.0.1

# Direct payments use a connected browser wallet and the fixed official network:
# Arc Testnet 5042002 / https://rpc.testnet.arc.io
# Native USDC uses 18 decimals; input accepts up to 6 decimal places.
# The app never reads a private-key environment variable or signs on the server.
# Legacy AP2/x402 examples and the server-side Arc adapter remain simulation-only.

# OPTIONAL independent human consent profile (public key only).
# Enroll on a separate human-controlled device, then set before starting the app.
# If set, each in-app payment requires a valid keyed counter-sign 0.2 receipt
# AND explicit external wallet approval. No human signing secret belongs here.
# COUNTERSIGN_APPROVER_PUBLIC_KEY=<canonical-base64url-raw-ed25519-public-key>
